  "rubrics": {
    "scope": "The events describe the priest-led Ordo. Ritus servandus V, 1 (editio typica 1962, p. LVII) has a bishop greet with Pax vobis when the Gloria has been said; episcopal forms are not described here. Ritus servandus VI, 5 (p. LVIII) and Rubricae generales 513 f (p. XXXV): at a solemn Mass the deacon says the Gospel greeting and the celebrant omits it. At a Missa cantata the celebrant sings it (Rubricae generales 514).",
    "secret": "Ritus servandus VII, 7 (p. LIX): the Secret is said without Orémus and without any other interposition, so no introduction precedes it.",
    "passion": "Dominica II Passionis seu in palmis, nn. 8 and 8 a (p. 136): the Passion begins without the Gospel greeting, and neither the book nor the reader is signed. The Gospel greeting does not precede it.",
    "easter-vigil": "Missa Vigiliae paschalis, rubric after the Gospel (p. 212): the celebrant says the greeting and Orémus, and no Offertory antiphon is said. The Offertory introduction stands without its antiphon.",
    "prayer-groups": "Ritus servandus V, 1 and XI, 1 give one introduction before the opening prayers and one before the prayers after Communion. Whether Orémus is said again before a second group of prayers is not settled by these pages and is not encoded here."
  }
}
